Each bay addresses a different dimension of caring for the dead:
The soul DEPARTS safely       → 大二爷伯 (escort)
The soul ARRIVES provisioned  → 阴财神 (material needs)
The soul is LIBERATED         → Dizang (soteriological)
Or reading the sequence differently — from the perspective of the living mourner performing ritual:
I BURN OFFERINGS for my ancestor
  → 阴财神 receives them and delivers material provisions

I PRAY TO DIZANG for my ancestor
  → Dizang intercedes to ease their suffering

I KNOW that at death
  → 大二爷伯 will escort the soul safely to the other side
The three bays answer the three questions that any living person concerned for their deceased relatives might ask: Did they get there safely? Are they suffering? Do they have what they need? Each bay addresses one question with a dedicated divine official.
